---
source: crates/leptoskit_admin/tests/admin.rs
expression: "redact(&world, &regions(&outline(&html), &[\"main\", \"drawer-aside\"]))"
---
main [main]
  div [notice] role=status
  div [analytics-not-configured]
    "Web analytics"
    div [empty-state]
      "Connect the admin to your analytics"
      "The admin is its own app, so it reads your site's analytics the way your site's server does: from the analytics service, signed with the service's token. It hasn't been given either yet. Set both where the admin runs, then reload:"
      div [code]
        div [code-line]
          span [code-text]
            "# Wherever the admin runs: the main site's analytics service,"
        div [code-line]
          span [code-text]
            "# at an address the admin can reach, and the token its server uses."
        div [code-line]
          span [code-text]
            "export LEPTOSKIT_SERVICE_ANALYTICS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4800"
        div [code-line]
          span [code-text]
            "export LEPTOSKIT_SERVICE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=…   # the same token as the site's server"
        div [code-line]
          span [code-text]
            "lk admin serve --main-site https://notes.example"
        button [copy] label="Copy as shell"
          "Copy"
      "The token is the app's: with it the admin can read every event, so keep it in the admin's environment, never in a page. AdminBuilder::analytics does the same from Rust."
    "Then, from your app"
    "once the service runs"
    "Your app sends events with a Rust type for each, so a misspelled property fails when it compiles rather than in a chart:"
    div [code]
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "use leptoskit_analytics::Event;"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "use leptoskit_analytics::client::web;"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "#[derive(Event)]"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "struct SignedUp {"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "plan: String,"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "seats: u32,"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "}"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "web::init(web::Options::default());"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "web::capture_event(SignedUp {"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "plan: \"pro\".into(),"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "seats: 3,"
      div [code-line]
        span [code-text]
          "});"
      button [copy] label="Copy as Rust"
        "Copy"
